  "sourceClauses": {
    "pdf:128:cell:15": "3.7.9.1 Near Branches in 64-Bit Mode",
    "pdf:128:cell:16": "The long-mode architecture expands the near-branch mechanisms to accommodate branches in the full",
    "pdf:128:cell:17": "64-bit virtual-address space. In 64-bit mode, the operand size for all near branches defaults to 64 bits,",
    "pdf:128:cell:18": "so these instructions update the full 64-bit RIP.",
    "pdf:128:cell:19": "Table 3-9 lists the near-branch instructions.",
    "pdf:128:cell:20": "Table 3-9. Near Branches in 64-Bit Mode",
    "pdf:128:cell:21": "Operand Size (bits)",
    "pdf:128:cell:22": "Mnemonic",
    "pdf:128:cell:23": "CALL",
    "pdf:128:cell:24": "Jcc",
    "pdf:128:cell:25": "JCXZ",
    "pdf:128:cell:26": "JECXZ",
    "pdf:128:cell:27": "JRCXZ",
    "pdf:128:cell:28": "JMP",
    "pdf:128:cell:29": "Opcode (hex)",
    "pdf:128:cell:30": "E8, FF /2",
    "pdf:128:cell:31": "Description",
    "pdf:128:cell:32": "Default",
    "pdf:128:cell:33": "Possible",
    "pdf:128:cell:34": "Overrides 1",
    "pdf:128:cell:35": "64",
    "pdf:128:cell:36": "16",
    "pdf:128:cell:37": "Call Procedure Near",
    "pdf:128:cell:38": "70 to 7F,",
    "pdf:128:cell:39": "Jump Conditional",
    "pdf:128:cell:40": "0F 80 to 0F 8F",
    "pdf:128:cell:41": "E3",
    "pdf:128:cell:42": "Jump on CX/ECX/RCX Zero",
    "pdf:128:cell:43": "EB, E9, FF /4 Jump Near",
    "pdf:128:cell:44": "LOOP",
    "pdf:128:cell:45": "E2",
    "pdf:128:cell:46": "Loop",
    "pdf:128:cell:47": "LOOPcc",
    "pdf:128:cell:48": "E0, E1",
    "pdf:128:cell:49": "Loop if Zero/Equal or Not Zero/Equal",
    "pdf:128:cell:50": "RET",
    "pdf:128:cell:51": "C2, C3",
    "pdf:128:cell:52": "Return From Call (near)",
    "pdf:128:cell:53": "Note:",
    "pdf:128:cell:54": "1. There is no 32-bit operand-size override prefix in 64-bit mode.",
    "pdf:128:cell:55": "The default 64-bit operand size eliminates the need for a REX prefix with these instructions when",
    "pdf:128:cell:56": "registers RAX\u2013RSP (the first set of eight GPRs) are used as operands. A REX prefix is still required if",
    "pdf:129:cell:10": "\u2022",
    "pdf:129:cell:11": "Size of a stack pop or push, resulting from a CALL or RET.",
    "pdf:129:cell:12": "Size of a stack-pointer increment or decrement, resulting from a CALL or RET.",
    "pdf:129:cell:13": "Indirect-branch operand size.",
    "pdf:129:cell:14": "In 64-bit mode, all of the above actions are forced to 64 bits. However, the size of the displacement",
    "pdf:129:cell:15": "field for relative branches is still limited to 32 bits.",
    "pdf:129:cell:16": "The operand size of near branches is fixed at 64 bits without the need for a REX prefix. However, the",
    "pdf:129:cell:17": "address size of near branches is not forced in 64-bit mode. Such addresses are 64 bits by default, but",
    "pdf:129:cell:18": "they can be overridden to 32 bits by a prefix.",
    "pdf:129:cell:3": "R8\u2013R15 (the extended set of eight GPRs) are used as operands, because the prefix is required to",
    "pdf:129:cell:4": "address the extended registers.",
    "pdf:129:cell:5": "The following aspects of near branches are controlled by the effective operand size:",
    "pdf:129:cell:6": "\u2022",
    "pdf:129:cell:7": "Truncation of the instruction pointer.",
    "pdf:129:cell:8": "\u2022",
    "pdf:129:cell:9": "\u2022"
  },
